The packages gitenv, sandbox and proc were first written in an earlier shared module of the same
authors, under the same licence, and were moved here unchanged in behaviour.

The library uses these modules, each under its own licence:

- golang.org/x/sys v0.49.0, which the library imports itself: the proc package on every system,
  the sandbox package for its Linux folder opens, the load package for macOS's load average and
  the service package for its Windows folder handles. golang.org/x/term and go-landlock require
  it too: BSD-3-Clause.
- golang.org/x/term v0.47.0, by which the proc package tells a terminal from a pipe or a file:
  BSD-3-Clause.
- github.com/shirou/gopsutil/v4 v4.26.10, by whose load.Avg the load package reads Linux's load
  average, its load, common and internal/common packages and no other in the build: BSD-3-Clause.
  The modules go.mod lists beside it for its other systems (ebitengine/purego, go-ole/go-ole,
  yusufpapurcu/wmi, power-devops/perfstat) are in no build of this library.
- github.com/landlock-lsm/go-landlock v0.11.2, through which the sandbox package sets its Linux
  folder rules: MIT.
- kernel.org/pub/linux/libs/security/libcap/psx v1.2.78, which go-landlock requires on Linux:
  BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0-only, taken here as BSD-3-Clause, the half its authors offer for
  permissive use, as Taskfile.yml's licenses task records.
- github.com/birdtable/go-testkit v0.3.1, of the same authors: the
  environment the library's tests run in, which the gitenv/gittest package, for tests alone,
  imports for its Clean. No other package of the library imports it: Apache-2.0.
